Reading:
- Composite C shells split into wide shallow channels and narrow redundant channels.
- At n=14, AP/Vstar/doubled_AP release 18 unit residues, 6 gcd-3 residues,
  and 2 gcd-9 residues when those channels are omitted; the gcd-9 residues
  are covered four times, so small mass can still be high-certainty structure.
- The prime C=23 control has one orbit: the raw bitmask has no shell-channel
  choice to damage, so side-channel scarcity appears only after lift/carry data.

