TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS: CHANNELS AND PROOF OBLIGATIONS
---------------------------------------------------
Vertices: channels/proof obligations, not LRC runners or unit-distance points.
Pairwise observable: which channel better preserves frontier decisions under impairment.
Switches: proof-relevance gauge versus scaling-value gauge.

proof gauge
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1, 7: 1, 8: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  scc_sizes=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
  hamiltonian_path_count=1
  tie Hamiltonian path:
    score=8 channel-complete ledger: keeps both scalar frontier and side channels
    score=7 LRC owner/carry/pinch fiber: reattaches the rare labels needed by n=14 quotient proofs
    score=6 UD gain-threshold solver: asks for gain-4/5 extension packets before geometry checks
    score=5 LRC witness-orbit jackknife: tests which C=2n-1 residue channels are load-bearing
    score=4 UD direction-drop jackknife: tests unit-shell indispensability by leave-one-direction-out
    score=3 UD canonical orbit budget: separates duplicate traffic from mathematical scarcity
    score=2 raw survival bitmask: fast LRC scalar frontier but forgets lift/carry proof data
    score=1 raw wider Moser beam: more compute without naming the retained invariant
    score=0 count-only quotient: same scalar count can be non-equivalent across channels

scaling gauge
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1, 7: 1, 8: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  scc_sizes=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
  hamiltonian_path_count=1
  tie Hamiltonian path:
    score=8 raw survival bitmask: fast LRC scalar frontier but forgets lift/carry proof data
    score=7 UD canonical orbit budget: separates duplicate traffic from mathematical scarcity
    score=6 UD gain-threshold solver: asks for gain-4/5 extension packets before geometry checks
    score=5 LRC witness-orbit jackknife: tests which C=2n-1 residue channels are load-bearing
    score=4 UD direction-drop jackknife: tests unit-shell indispensability by leave-one-direction-out
    score=3 channel-complete ledger: keeps both scalar frontier and side channels
    score=2 raw wider Moser beam: more compute without naming the retained invariant
    score=1 count-only quotient: same scalar count can be non-equivalent across channels
    score=0 LRC owner/carry/pinch fiber: reattaches the rare labels needed by n=14 quotient proofs

