ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE
--------------------
Alternate vertices considered: LRC runners, LRC witness residues, shell/gcd
strata, owner routes, carry cocycles, unit-distance points, unit directions,
gain packets, deletion cores, canonical orbit classes, obstruction filters,
and proof obligations.
Chosen vertices: channels/proof obligations, because the preserved predicate
is whether a damaged method changes the frontier decision.
Information preserved: C-tick survival response, witness-orbit release mass,
Moser direction loss, gain-ceiling loss, and channel ranking under two gauges.
Information destroyed: exact continuous LRC time geometry, arbitrary integer
lift provenance, full unit-distance embedding outside the finite carrier, and
proof-grade totally-unfaithful obstruction certificates.
Challenged assumption: widening a frontier-gain beam is the next unit of
progress.  The bridge table says widen only after naming the side channel that
the width is preserving.

